# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch B."""
DESC_B = {
    "RT": {
        12: """Appeared in Episode 4, 'Young Blood Burns Crimson,' a Saucer Beast sent to locate Grendizer's base.
It indiscriminately destroyed the city with spikes launched from its saucer section and flames breathed from its mouth. It was also equipped with an electromagnetic net, which it used to shoot down a TFO.""",
        13: """Appeared from Episode 73, 'For This Beautiful Earth,' the strongest and last Vega Beast, piloted personally by Lady Gandal.
It tormented Grendizer with weapons such as a blinding ray fired from the protrusions on its chest and scorching flames breathed from its mouth.""",
        14: """Flagship of the united Vega star forces, named for Emperor Vega himself. Like the TFO, it is believed to have taken its design motif from the cigar-shaped UFOs that were famous at the time.
When the all-out attack on Earth began, Emperor Vega personally took command and sortied aboard it.""",
        15: """The form completed when the Get Machines combine in the order Dragon, Liger, and Poseidon. As with Getter 1, the pilot remains Ryouma Nagare.
Unlike the old Getter, which was originally built for space development, this Getter was designed from the start for combat. With the installation of a Getter Ray Amplifier, it became capable of generating over ten times the power of the old Getter. Its armor, made of Synthetic Element Steel G, was also made far more durable.
It excelled in aerial combat, using the 'Getter Beam' at range and the 'Double Tomahawk' up close, along with the 'Mach Wing' on its back. It is the only form that can use Getter's ultimate finishing move, the 'Shine Spark,' and it defeated countless powerful foes with it.""",
        16: """The form completed when the Get Machines combine in the order Liger, Poseidon, and Dragon. As with Getter 2, the pilot remains Hayato Jin.
Unlike the old Getter, which was originally built for space development, this Getter was designed from the start for combat. With the installation of a Getter Ray Amplifier, it became capable of generating over ten times the power of the old Getter. Its armor, made of Synthetic Element Steel G, was also made far more durable.
Of the three Getter forms, it boasts the greatest speed, and uses the 'Mach Special' to create illusory doubles that confuse its foes. Its left arm can be launched as a 'Chain Arm' or unfolded to fire the 'Raiga Missile.' Its right arm can transform into a drill, letting it attack as well as tunnel through the ground.""",
        17: """The form completed when the Get Machines combine in the order Poseidon, Dragon, and Liger. Benkei Kurama serves as its pilot, replacing Musashi Tomoe, who died fighting the Dinosaur Empire.
Unlike the old Getter, which was originally built for space development, this Getter was designed from the start for combat. With the installation of a Getter Ray Amplifier, it became capable of generating over ten times the power of the old Getter. Its armor, made of Synthetic Element Steel G, was also made far more durable.
Of the three Getter forms, it possesses the greatest power, showing its true worth in close-quarters combat using weapons like the 'Finger Net.' It excels most at underwater activity, and by transforming both legs into caterpillar treads, it can easily traverse even the harshest terrain on the seafloor.""",
        18: """Michiru Saotome's new mount, replacing the Command Machine.
Being lightweight, it has somewhat limited durability, but excels in mobility.
It served in a support role, providing covering fire with 'Command Missiles,' scouting with its onboard electronics, and resupplying the Getter Robo.""",
        19: """A fighter craft of the Hyakki Empire, crewed by common troops known as Hyakki soldiers.
It mainly supports Hyakki mechs, though it sometimes serves as the mainstay of an operation. A bomber-type variant also exists.""",
        20: """Appeared from Episode 1, 'Getter Robo Reborn!!,' a Hyakki mech piloted by Ikkakuki.
Beyond the giant blade on one arm, its weapons are varied, including a ray fired from its eyes and a beam launched from its horn.
As a vanguard of the Hyakki Empire, it attacked the Saotome Institute to seize the Getter Ray Amplifier. Against the Getter Team, who were not yet accustomed to their new Getter Robo, it resorted to the cowardly tactic of taking Genki hostage.""",
        21: """Appeared in Episode 2, 'The Fearsome Riddle of the Hyakki Empire,' a Hyakki mech piloted by Dokuganki.
It can tunnel through the ground by spinning the Hook Claws on both hands, and it planned to attack the Saotome Institute from underground.""",
        22: """Appeared in Episode 16, 'Death Match! A Man's Path Through the Storm,' a Hyakki mech developed personally by Tekkoki.
Having thoroughly studied Getter Robo, its performance is formidable, and it tormented the Getter Team greatly with weaponry nearly identical to Getter Robo's own, including a Tomahawk.""",
        23: """Appeared in Episode 35, 'Old Hyakki Soldiers Never Die,' a Hyakki mech piloted by Gyukenki.
Beyond his battle-hardened swordsmanship, he cornered the Getter with techniques such as the 'Hyakki Typhoon' blown from his mouth.""",
        24: """Appeared from Episode 20, 'All-Out Attack! Mecha Yosaiki,' an aircraft-carrier-type Hyakki mech.
It can carry two Hyakki mechs on its left and right wings, along with 100 bombers and 200 fighters inside its body. It used its overwhelming firepower to bomb Tokyo and destroy the Saotome Institute.""",
        25: """Appeared from Episode 37, 'Crisis Looms in Japan's Coastal Waters!,' the strongest Hyakki mech, formed by combining five units: Mecha Kokakuki, Mecha Anchuki, Mecha Rinmaki, Mecha Raijuki, and Mecha Juppoki.
It boasts overwhelming power, and can also separate back into its individual Hyakki mechs after combining.""",
        26: """The Hyakki Empire's home base, built using their own unique science and technology. Its armor is sturdy enough to repel Getter's attacks.
It normally floats on the ocean's surface, but its ability to travel underwater made it difficult to locate. Inside, Hyakki soldiers are modified and Hyakki mechs are developed.
Using the gravity control device left behind by Dr. Gura, it also gained the ability to fly, and during the final battle it attacked Tokyo from the sky.""",
        27: """A giant robot belonging to Blue Fixer, born of the combined scientific might of Planet S-1 and Earth.
Blue Fixer recovered the Pulsavarn after it drifted ashore on the Moon. They then pooled all their available technology to modify it so it could combine with two Earth combat machines, creating the only machine on Earth's side capable of subspace combat. Like the Pulsavarn, it can only be piloted by Marin, an expert in subspace mechanics.
Combination begins with Marin's call of "Baldios, charge up!" It is completed when the Pulsavarn forms the head, torso, and arms, the Baldi Prise forms the right leg, and the Cat Ranger forms the left leg.
It is powered by three engines - a deuterium fusion engine, an anti-gravity engine, and a subspace propulsion engine - and by switching between them, it can operate anywhere. Its speed within the atmosphere is Mach 25; in space it can fly at 30% the speed of light, and within subspace, at infinite speed.
Its main weapons include the 'Bal Beam,' fired from the crystal on its forehead, the 'Pulse Saber,' a sword stored in a chest component, and the 'Thunder Flash,' which fires intense plasma from its chest.""",
        28: """A spacecraft built to destroy the moon Ganymede, which the Aldebaron forces had moved into position between Earth and the Sun. In truth it was not a spacecraft at all, but a suicide weapon with a 0% survival rate - its pilot would have no time to escape before being caught in Ganymede's explosion.
Because the speed reached the speed of light when the launch boosters were jettisoned in space, piloting it required subspace-mechanics knowledge and piloting skill equal to Marin's own.
Knowing full well she would never survive, Marin volunteered as pilot. But David, who had been assigned to Blue Fixer as a candidate pilot for the New Pulsavarn, also volunteered, and in the end he was the one chosen.""",
        29: """The main combat fighter of the Aldebaron forces.
Its armament consists of only two laser cannons, but combined with its high mobility and its subspace-entry device, it gave the World Federation forces - who had no means of entering subspace themselves - a hard time.
It is used for every kind of mission, from reconnaissance to interception. Countless units have also been known to combine into a giant manta ray.""",
        30: """Appeared in Episode 4, 'The Day of the Subspace Dive,' the Aldebaron forces' first Earth-attack mech.
It normally has an egg-like shape, but transforms into this form for battle, capturing foes within its tentacles and damaging them with electric shocks.""",
        31: """Appeared in Episode 27, 'The Spy I Believed In,' an ultra-reactive robot developed by Aphrodia.
Its main weapons are the rays fired from its eyes and chest, and an attack in which it launches its forearms.
It possesses the ability to predict its opponent's actions, and by dodging every attack, it tormented Baldios just after its power-up.""",
        32: """Appeared in Episode 30, 'The Day Earth Turned Barren,' a combat mech of the Aldebaron forces.
It appeared over grain belts across the world, spraying a sterilizing agent of unknown material composition and plunging Earth into a food crisis. It can transform between an airplane form for spraying the agent and a robot form for combat.
Beyond its 'Destruction Ray,' it carries a close-combat weapon that spins four blades from its waist at high speed.""",
        33: """The main battleship of the Aldebaron forces.
Capable of operating in both subspace and three-dimensional space, it is a mobile base that can carry 117 Transparent Saucers. Nearly all of Earth's conquest operations were carried out using this carrier, and Aphrodia used one of them as her flagship.
Its armament includes laser cannons, particle cannons, and missiles.""",
        34: """A mech used in the operation to annihilate humanity, seen in the final episode, 'Prelude to Destruction (Part 1).'
Two units were built - one melted the ice at the North Pole, the other at the South Pole, causing massive flooding across the Earth.
Once activated, it has the ability to convert any attack against it into its own energy. Because of this, Blue Fixer could only watch helplessly as the ice melted away. Facing the oncoming tsunami, Commander Tsukikage came to regret that he had been too wary of a trap and hesitated to attack before it activated.""",
        35: """Aldebaron's flagship.
In the unaired Episode 34, 'The Long Afternoon of Earth,' Gattler himself boarded it and took command at the front lines.
It possesses formidable combat power, and no battleship exists - not on Earth, nor even within the Aldebaron forces - that can compare to it. Given its sharply angular appearance, it is believed to hold the power to destroy even a planet.""",
        36: """A robot developed by Dr. Kazami. Also called Robot No. 1.
When combining into God Sigma, it forms the parts from the knees up, and it is equipped with a special system that prevents anyone unsuited to be its pilot from operating it.
Its weapons include the 'Rivet Gun,' which fires a variety of rivet rounds, the 'Kurai Shot,' which launches energy like a slingshot, and the 'Kurai Shock,' which discharges electricity from its shoulders. It is also equipped with numerous other projectile weapons beyond these.""",
        37: """A super robot developed by Dr. Kazami.
KuRaiOh forms the upper body, KaiMeiOh the right leg, and RikuShinOh the left leg; Big Wing then combines over KuRaiOh to cover the chest and back, completing the super robot God Sigma, which runs on Trinity Energy as its power source.
Normally the three pilots of KuRaiOh, KaiMeiOh, and RikuShinOh remain in control as-is, but it is also possible for the pilot of KuRaiOh alone to operate it. In that case, however, the power of KaiMeiOh and RikuShinOh cannot be fully utilized, which is a drawback.
Its armament includes the 'Finger Needle,' which fires energy bolts from its fingertips, the 'God Tomahawk,' which can be thrown or wielded by hand, and the 'Spin Saucer,' a spiked disc thrown with a sidearm motion. Its finishing move is a series of swordsmanship techniques using the 'Musou Sword' stored in Big Wing. Its many variations include the 'Bamboo Splitter,' 'Reverse Diagonal Cut,' 'Cross Cut,' 'Helmet Splitter,' 'Horizontal Cut,' 'Double-Edged Thrust,' 'Double-Edged Return Cut,' 'Two-Handed Cut,' 'Lightning Cut,' and 'Straight Cut,' among others - a truly varied repertoire.""",
        38: """A fighter craft of the Elder forces.
Mostly crewed by rank-and-file soldiers, it is deployed in operations that favor quantity over quality.
On one occasion, Toshiya skillfully piloted a unit captured by KaiMeiOh's Net Catcher, using it to sow confusion among the enemy.""",
        39: """Appeared from Episode 1, 'Warriors of Io, Rise in Anger,' Cosmosaurus No. 1.
It attacked Trinity City with a variety of destruction rays and its ability to generate whirlpools.""",
        40: """A Cosmosaurus that appeared in Episode 19, 'Robot Unable to Launch.'
With an appearance reminiscent of a giant carnivorous dinosaur, its bone-crushing hug attack, delivered from a body even larger than God Sigma's, is formidable.""",
        41: """A Cosmosaurus with the body of a hedgehog and the face of a bat, appearing in Episode 38, 'Departure for Io.'
By infiltrating from beneath the seabed, it nullified Trinity Base's barrier and attacked it from within using electric-shock missiles and 'Solvent Missiles.'""",
        42: """A space battleship used by the Elder forces in their conquest of Earth.
It is equipped with powerful weaponry such as missiles and beams, and is operated at the front lines by Reeds and others.""",
        43: """A giant robot piloted by Gagaan, appearing in the final episode, 'Departure for the Future.'
It was formed when the surface of Gagaan's fortress collapsed and the glowing object within transformed.
It possesses a body far larger than God Sigma's and armor sturdy enough to withstand even the Sigma Breast. Wielding an axe in its right hand and a morning star in its left, it breathed fire from its mouth and fired penetrating lasers from the eight holes in its chest, overwhelming God Sigma.""",
        44: """A super robot developed by the Beal aliens to fight the Gaizock.
Three mechs - Zambird, forming the head and chest; Zambull, forming the arms and abdomen; and Zambase, forming the waist and legs - combine into a giant robot embodying justice and mystery with the call, "Zambot Combination In!"
Combining activates its ion engine, generating power truly worthy of the name 'Invincible Superman.' Its main weapons include the 'Zambot Grap,' a trident blade extending from its arms, the cross-shaped shuriken 'Zambot Buster' on its knees, and the 'Buster Missile,' fired from that same shuriken's spikes. Its ultimate finishing move, the 'Zambot Moon Attack,' fires a crescent-shaped energy bolt from the horn on its head, and it has several different signature poses for using it.""",
        45: """A high-speed fighter developed by the Beal aliens to fight the Gaizock.
It combines with Zambull and Zambase to form Zambot 3, providing its head and chest. On its own, it can also transform into the small robot form 'Zambo Ace.'
Its armament includes the nose-mounted vulcan cannon 'Bird Gun' and the shockwave cannon 'Torenburu Horn.' Though unused in the show, it also carries weapons such as large missiles and cluster rockets.""",
        46: """A robot developed by the Beal aliens to fight the Gaizock.
It is a small, close-combat-focused robot form into which Zambird transforms when its pilot Kappei shouts, "Ace Change!"
Its primary weapon is the 'Zambo Magnum,' which flies in on autopilot from King Beal. Combined with optional equipment, it can also be used as a rifle or to fire grenades.
Its cockpit is located in the somewhat unusual position of the tips of both feet.""",
        47: """A reconnaissance Mecha Boost appearing in Episode 1, 'Enter Zambo Ace.'
It can tunnel through the ground using the blades on the tips of its tentacles, and it also fires a laser from its mouth and Homing Missiles from its waist.""",
        48: """A Mecha Boost that attacked refugees in the Yokkaichi region, appearing in Episode 7, 'Farewell, My Friend.'
It breathes flames laced with poison gas from its mouth, discharges barbed wire carrying an electric current from its pincers, and fires drills and missiles from its forehead.
In its first battle, with Zambase absent and unable to combine, it gave Zambo Ace and Zambull a hard fight.""",
        49: """A Mecha Boost that attacked the evacuation ship carrying Aki, appearing in Episode 18, 'Aki and Kappei.'
It tormented Zambo Ace with beams from its eyes, electric shocks from the tentacles on its arms, and a spinning charge attack using its lower body.""",
        50: """A Mecha Boost that sortied to protect Bandock, appearing in Episode 21, 'Showdown! The Jin Family.'
It fires missiles from the huge barrel on its head, particle lasers from both shoulders powerful enough to cancel out the Moon Attack, and wires from the spiked iron ball at the tip of its tail.""",
        51: """Its official name is 'Red Knight Deathcain.'
One of the Knights of Death, appearing in Episode 22, 'Butcher's Last Day.'
It wields a massive machete that fires a beam from its tip. By combining its shield with that of its counterpart, the Blue Knight Helldyne, it can also create weapons such as swords and iron balls.""",
        52: """Its official name is 'Blue Knight Helldyne.'
One of the Knights of Death, appearing in Episode 22, 'Butcher's Last Day.'
It wields a massive lance that fires a beam from its tip. By combining its shield with that of its counterpart, the Red Knight Deathcain, it can also create weapons such as swords and iron balls.""",
        53: """A mobile fortress that serves as the Gaizock's home base.
It can operate anywhere - on land, underwater, or in space - and its interior houses Butcher's command room as well as a Mecha Boost production factory.
It fires 'Bandokku Cannons' from both arms, large missiles from its mouth, and 'Destruction Rays' from its eyes, and also attacks with space mines and its extendable legs. It can generate a powerful barrier and boasts high defensive strength. Its head can also separate from the main body for independent use, as it did when Butcher personally led an attack.""",
        54: """A mobile base boarded by the Jin family to fight the Gaizock.
It is completed when Beal I through III combine: the Jin family's Beal I forms the stern, the Kamie family's Beal II forms both sides, and the Kamikita family's Beal III forms the bow.
It is equipped with missiles, laser cannons, and barrier cannons, and can also fire a powerful 'Ion Cannon.' It was originally an immigrant spaceship built by the Beal aliens 150 years ago, and was not designed for combat.""",
        55: """A super robot completed when Banjo seized a prototype Megaborg developed on Mars by Souzou Haran and modified it.
It has a three-stage transformation mechanism, able to change into the heavy fighter-bomber Daifighter and the heavy tank Daitank. It houses the small variable fighter Mach Attacker inside, and that unit's cockpit block moves through the machine's body to become Daitarn 3's pilot seat.
Its main weapons include the beam-bladed sword 'Daitarn Zanbar,' the fan-shaped 'Daitarn Fan,' which can also be used as a shield, and the 'Daitarn Web,' whose arm-mounted cross transforms into a shuriken. Beyond these, it carries numerous other weapons built into its whole body, including missiles, cannons, and snappers.
Its ultimate finishing move, the 'Sun Attack,' fires a bolt of light from the sun disc on its forehead with the call, "Lend me the power of the sun - now, my finishing blow, Sun Attack!" Other variations of this call also exist, and on occasion the call was made without the attack actually being fired.""",
        56: """Daitarn 3's fighter-bomber form.
When Banjo shouts "Daitarn, come here!" into his small communicator, it flies in from far away in this form. After taking the Mach Attacker aboard, it transforms into Daitarn 3 in response to the call, "Change, Daitarn!"
It can fly at Mach 20 within the atmosphere and near light-speed in space. From other forms, it transforms with the call, "Change, Daifighter!\"""",
        57: """Daitarn 3's tank form.
It transforms with the call, "Change, Daitank!" and is used on rough terrain and underground. Its main weapon is the 'Daitarn Cannon,' fired from its legs.""",
        58: """The machine completed when Kei's beloved mount, the Bronco II, was severely damaged and, during repairs, was reinforced and modified using Emaan technology.
The Bronco II's legs were kept as they were, while its arms were replaced at Kei's request, since he had liked the handling of the M.Lover's arms when he piloted it. Furthermore, by adding a psycho system along with three inertial control systems, two anti-gravity levitation devices, and a nuclear reactor with output approaching 500,000 horsepower, it came to surpass the performance of the old Drifand despite being a hastily assembled machine. Thanks to its high performance, a mass-production model was later developed as well.
Beyond its robot form, the Orgaroid, another major feature is its shape-shifting capability (VARIABLE GEOMETRY), which lets it take four forms as the situation demands: Flyer, GERWALK, and Tank.
When it was completed, there was a scene in which the members of the Factory discussed what to call the new Bronco II, with everyone freely proposing names like 'Valhalla' and 'Gammon.' In the end, it was named 'Orguss,' after the name of a god of war from the world Jabby came from. Incidentally, 'Nebulard,' one of the proposed names, was the show's working title during its planning stage.""",
        59: """The aerial combat and cruising form of Kei's Orguss.
It boasts greater mobility than the Bronco II, but because the sky above is covered by the Realm of Conflict, issues such as an altitude ceiling kept it from ever displaying that mobility to the full. Even so, Kei's exceptional piloting sense gave it the chance to shine on many different battlefields.""",
        60: """One of the mass-production Orguss units developed in the Emaan homeland after its performance was recognized. This is the machine piloted by Olson, who had taken refuge with the Factory. It differs from both the standard mass-production units and Kei's Orguss in its color scheme and the shape of its head and legs.
To ease its handling difficulty, the mass-production units' engines were fitted with a limiter, but on Olson's unit, that limiter was removed in consideration of his piloting skill. As a result, it is the highest-performing machine among all those bearing the Orguss name.""",
        61: """The aerial combat and cruising form of Olson's Orguss II.
It holds output and mobility that even surpass the original Orguss, but for the same reason as the Orguss, it was rarely given the chance to fly at full power.""",
    },
}
